There have been two instances where stupid mailman got a bounce from somewhere
and decided to unsubscribe a whole bunch of people from a UML list.  It
happened to ~50 people on uml-devel last week, and ~90 on uml-user today.

I resubscribed everyone.  However, I think I accidentally put some uml-devel
people on uml-user due to me messing up a grep and getting some addresses
from the uml-devel fiasco last week.  Also, you may have been resubscribed
with different options than you want.

If you're on a list you didn't want to be or your list options are wrong,
go to one of the following places to fix yourself up:

	https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/user-mode-linux-user
	https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/user-mode-linux-devel

Sorry for any bother this causes.

				Jeff



